\draw (4,-1) node[circle,draw] {{\tiny 3}};




\draw[arrows={-latex}, very thick] (.25,1) -- (3.8,1);
\draw[arrows={-latex}, very thick] (.25,0) -- (3.8,0);
\draw[arrows={-latex}, very thick] (.25,-1) -- (3.75,-1);

\draw (4,-2.75) node {Y= [3]};

\end{tikzpicture}



Required Relationship:  n = m












 Create a function f: [n] \rightarrow [m] that is NOT injective (one-to-one) but is surjective (onto). What is the required relationship between n and m? (One of: n  >m or n < m or n = m or "none.")







